(F5 T6 U4: control_safety_slip 3, refinement of a multi linear zone. 4x4 quad4 mesh, uniform strain: sigxx = sigyy = -1, sigxy = 0.5,
 Mohr-Coulomb c 1, phi 30 deg (elastic); a line at angle t:
 Fs = (1 + (1 + 0.5 sin 2t) tan phi) / (0.5 |cos 2t|).
 Lines (0.5,2.5)-(3.5,1.5) to (0.5,1.5)-(3.5,2.6), _n 3, 4 points per
 piece. Each pass after the first takes the critical line so far plus and
 minus a part of the step of every coordinate: half a step after pass 1,
 a quarter of a step after the later passes (measured on the Professional
 02-08-2026). 9 surfaces; critical surface 8 = line (0.5, 2.1875)-
 (3.5, 1.84375), Fs 3.1045712104 (Professional 3.104571210375).
 Pass 1 critical: the middle line, Fs 3.1757039931.)
